1
00:00:00,040 --> 00:00:03,480
Step number five run towards failure.
第五步：迎着失败走。

2
00:00:03,480 --> 00:00:09,720
One thing I've seen is that our generation gets so embarrassed and gets the ick so easily.
我注意到的一件事是，我们这一代很容易觉得丢脸，也很容易产生反感。

3
00:00:09,720 --> 00:00:13,870
And I feel like it's preventing us from learning so much about ourselves and about the world.
我觉得，这让我们错过了很多认识自己、认识世界的机会。

4
00:00:13,880 --> 00:00:16,990
Which is inevitably going to get us further than everybody else right.
而这些认识，本来最终会让我们比其他人走得更远，对吧？

5
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:23,160
Listen I am all for high standards but high standards that are earned through your lived experience.
听着，我完全支持有高标准，但那些标准应该来自你亲身经历过的生活。

6
00:00:23,160 --> 00:00:27,959
Because think about it this way you have learned so much from your breakups from your friend endings.
因为你这样想想：你已经从分手、从友谊的结束中学到了那么多。

7
00:00:27,959 --> 00:00:32,600
So how dare you feel embarrassed about them they literally got you to where you are.
所以你怎么能因此觉得丢脸呢？正是这些经历把你带到了今天的位置。

8
00:00:32,600 --> 00:00:37,480
They literally made you the person you are stronger than ever wiser than ever more knowledgeable than ever.
正是这些经历造就了今天的你：比以往更坚强、更明智，也更有见识。

9
00:00:37,480 --> 00:00:44,920
Those experiences are literally what gifted you your high standards they taught you what to look for in people in jobs in your hobbies.
正是那些经历让你有了高标准，也教会你在交往对象、工作和爱好中应该看重什么。

10
00:00:44,920 --> 00:00:49,079
So you know people say I don't know myself or my passions or what I want to do.
所以，你知道，有人说：“我不了解自己，不知道自己的热情在哪里，也不知道自己想做什么。”

11
00:00:49,079 --> 00:00:52,280
It's because you haven't lived enough to find out what they truly are.
那是因为你还没有经历足够多的生活，去发现那些真正是什么。

12
00:00:52,280 --> 00:00:55,720
It's not just going to come to you randomly by sitting in your bedroom scrolling on tiktok.
答案不会仅仅因为你坐在卧室里刷 TikTok，就突然随机出现。

13
00:00:55,720 --> 00:01:02,519
Because self discovery is messy and it's chaotic and it's trying 10 things you absolutely hate just to find the one thing that you really love.
因为自我探索是混乱的、没有秩序的；它意味着尝试十件你特别讨厌的事，只为找到那件你真正热爱的事。

14
00:01:02,519 --> 00:01:06,440
And also even through the 10 things that you hate finding out so much about yourself.
而且，即使是通过那十件你不喜欢的事，你也能发现很多关于自己的东西。

15
00:01:06,440 --> 00:01:10,840
Your limits what you love what you want to do what you absolutely want to remove out of your life.
你的极限在哪里，你喜欢什么，想做什么，以及你特别想从生活中去掉什么。

16
00:01:10,840 --> 00:01:14,600
That's magic and that's such a gift to be able to learn at such a young age.
这很神奇，能在这么年轻的时候学到这些，是多么宝贵的一份收获。

17
00:01:14,600 --> 00:01:20,600
So remember your dream life won't be delivered to you while you're hiding from embarrassment it will be built through it.
所以请记住：你躲着丢脸的时候，梦想的生活不会送上门；它会在你经历这些尴尬的过程中建立起来。

18
00:01:20,600 --> 00:01:25,320
Number six communication skills is going to make the rest of your life so much easier.
第六点：沟通技巧会让你今后的生活轻松得多。

19
00:01:25,320 --> 00:01:31,880
When it comes to making friends making good impressions getting opportunities and jobs connecting with people and growing more as a person.
比如交朋友、留下好印象、得到机会和工作、与人建立联系，以及让自己成长得更多。

20
00:01:31,880 --> 00:01:40,440
So by communication skills I mean emotional intelligence being a good listener understanding the importance of small talk versus deep chats.
所以我说的沟通技巧，包括情商、做一个好的倾听者，以及理解闲聊和深入交谈各自的重要性。

21
00:01:40,440 --> 00:01:48,519
And knowing when to employ both communication skills and conflict literally the key to good long lasting healthy relationships and setting boundaries.
还有知道什么时候运用这两种方式。沟通技巧以及冲突处理，按她的说法，是建立良好、长久、健康关系和设定边界的关键。

22
00:01:48,519 --> 00:01:53,310
It all comes down to those communication skills and hey even if you don't want to take my word for it.
归根结底，这些都与沟通技巧有关。而且，即使你不愿意只听我这么说。

23
00:01:53,320 --> 00:02:03,320
Mit researchers have literally said your ability to detect tone micro expressions and emotional cues determines your success more than your iq.
作者接着声称，MIT 研究人员说过，你识别语气、微表情和情绪信号的能力，比智商更能决定成功。

24
00:02:03,320 --> 00:02:08,759
Need I say more so how can you master this I've actually read quite a few books on this that completely changed my life.
还需要我多说吗？那么，你怎样掌握这些呢？我读过不少这方面的书，它们彻底改变了我的生活。

25
00:02:08,759 --> 00:02:13,079
And hey all of this advice is coming from a formerly socially awkward girl who was such an introvert.
而且，这些建议都来自一个以前社交很笨拙、特别内向的女孩。

26
00:02:13,079 --> 00:02:18,040
I used to hate communicating with people I hate conflict I'm a libra okay.
我以前讨厌与人交流，我讨厌冲突；我是天秤座，好吧。

27
00:02:18,040 --> 00:02:22,360
I didn't want to go up to people and start conversations and make friends it literally made me want to crawl into a hole.
我不想主动走向别人、开启对话、交朋友；这些事简直让我想找个洞钻进去。

28
00:02:22,360 --> 00:02:26,519
I would literally do anything I would stay in my house for the rest of my life rather than doing any of those things.
我简直什么都愿意做；我宁愿一辈子待在家里，也不愿做那些事情。

29
00:02:26,519 --> 00:02:31,240
But I knew I was hurting and damaging my own potential by not learning how to do those things.
但我知道，不去学习做这些事，是在伤害、损耗我自己的潜力。

30
00:02:31,240 --> 00:02:36,120
So you should read books like how to win friends and influence people and how to talk to anyone.
所以，你应该读一些书，比如《人性的弱点》和《如何与任何人交谈》。

31
00:02:36,120 --> 00:02:41,949
Oh and another book it's called surrounded by idiots that's also a really good one at just understanding different types of people.
哦，还有另一本，叫《身边的白痴》；她认为，在理解不同类型的人这方面，那也是一本很好的书。

32
00:02:41,959 --> 00:02:49,959
Seven my favorite one love is the last thing you should worry about especially before the age of 25.
第七点，我最喜欢的一点：爱情应该是你最不需要操心的事，尤其在二十五岁以前。

33
00:02:49,959 --> 00:03:00,189
If it comes to you naturally accidentally amazing enjoy it but if you are searching for it you are abandoning the most important relationship you are ever going to have.
如果爱情自然地、偶然地出现，那太好了，去享受吧。但如果你一直寻找它，作者认为你是在忽略一生中最重要的关系。

34
00:03:00,199 --> 00:03:08,120
The relationship you have with yourself living alone thriving independently surviving heartbreak making friends on your own exploring the world on your own.
也就是你与自己的关系：独自生活、独立过得很好、走过心碎、自己交朋友、独自探索世界。

35
00:03:08,120 --> 00:03:15,240
Traveling growing your finances growing your self love building up your self image and self perception those are the real flexes.
旅行、改善财务状况、增长自爱、建立自我形象和自我认知——作者说，这些才是真正值得自豪的事。

36
00:03:15,240 --> 00:03:18,400
Marriage having a wedding that can come at literally any time.
至于婚姻、办婚礼，那些在任何时候都可以到来。
